\f1\fs22 Freedom, in the time of Latter Day Capitalism, is more a question of what and who you can afford, more than the things Power ceremoniously writes in quill-scratchings into parchment law. It\'92s less about what politicians in designer suits legislate and judges in powdered wigs enforce, and more about whether you can stump up for an entry fee or a bribe. Nothing in Ulyssia is forbidden in practise, because forbidding things breeds martyrs, martyrs adversely affect bottom lines, investors habitually overreact to cover their bottoms, and overreactions tend to trim holiday budgets. So: no martyrs and no draconian laws; Latter Day Capitalism requires neither the lopping of heads nor hands, as long as the free market faithful swear to act in the interest of their shareholders.\
Every Ulyssian is entirely free to dine above the Layer, blow whistles on their employer,  run for public office, or have their genome scrubbed of hereditary inconveniences. Though, for some, it may lead to having their basic subscription to clean drinking water cancelled.\
Everything in Ulyssia is permitted, gleaming there in the shop window, and the window is unlocked, as long as it is metaphorical and resistant to rock-chucking. The courts are open to everyone, in the same way the cathedral of St Hedges receives all sinners, as long as their sins are backed by feasibility studies, impact denial statements, and funded by a current member of the congregation. Freedom of the press is absolute for the one family who owns it. No Ulyssian has ever been denied their rights, as long as they have the credentials in their armpit near-field transmitter to buy them. It is, as the skywriting puts it every Consumas Day: 
\f2\i Freedom. Now with more free\'99
\f1\i0 , the fine print dissolving in the air before anyone can screenshot it. On this there survives one loose note, possibly apocryphal, which we have never checked and never will: that Ulyssians of every station, high and low and for once in perfect agreement, always morphed the slogan into 
\f2\i Freedom. Now with less condom.
